ated short along  with background painter Eric Radomski  Tim and Radomski developed a minute and  a half long short to depict a Batman  thwarting an attempted jewelry robbery  and featured a cameo appearance by  Commissioner Jim Gordon mccurdy was so  impressed with the short as she put him  a Radomski in charge of developing an  entire series featuring the distinct  simplistic animation style in doing so  burst him set out to create an entire  series that would differ from the rest  of the cartoons in production at the  time and that it would appeal to not  only children but to adults as well  to do this an entire team of like-minded  creators needed to be assembled and so  another former hanna-barbera writer of  producer Alan Burnett joined the Batman  creative team Burnett had worked with DC  superheroes before as a writer on Super  Friends and had also written 50 episodes  of the Smurfs and worked on many of DC's  animated series in the 1990s before  coming to warner brothers  initially Burnett had no interest in  working on Batman because he'd been  frustrated with the strict standards and  practices that controlled cartoon  programming however after seeing the  shore that's him in Radomski had created  he became convinced that the Batman  series would be a faithful adaptation to  the character and agreed to go on board  also joining the team was writer Paul  Dini who'd worked with Tim on Tiny Toons  Dini had tried unsuccessfully to break  in a comic book writing in the past and  was eager to get to work on the Batman  project and so one of the first things  that Tim Burnett and Dini did along with  writer Mitch Bryan was develop a show  Bible or blueprint for the narrative and  a synthetic vision of the show that  would guide the production of future  episodes for his part Dini drew  inspiration from seminal Batman works  such as Frank Miller's Batman year one  and Alan Moore's The Killing Joke  Burnett was also committed to keeping  the show true to the essence of the  Batman mythos while at the same time  being fun for kids to watch which also  meant leaving out aliens and ghosts and  avoiding heavy social issues the team  soon added Shirley Walker a composer  who'd worked on the 1989 Batman film to  score each episode of the series a  practice that was practically unheard of  among animated series at the time and so  his Cassie began over 120 actors chosen  from a pool of 500 submitted recordings  were auditioned voice director Andrea  Romano had narrowed the pool down to  four actors but none of them quite  captured what she was looking for she  asked her roommate a casting director if  he knew any actors who would be good for  the role and he suggested a Juilliard  educated stage and soap opera actor  named Kevin Conroy  although Conway had never done any voice  acting up to that point Romano had  brought him in for an audition and was  blown away by Conway's work Bruce Timm  was also impressed citing the distinct  voices Conway had created for both  Batman and Bruce Wayne as one of the  factors that led to his selection for  the role  I am the knight and so once the team had  found their Batman  the next task was finding the right  voice for Batman's arch nemesis the  Joker  according to boost him the vast majority  of the applicants tried to emulate Cesar  Romero's portrayal in the 1966 Batman  television series starring Adam West  which was not what the showrunners had  in mind for the primary villain  eventually the team settled on Tim Curry  who was an experienced voice and film  actor but after recording a few episodes  they realized that curry did not fit  their vision and they began to consider  recasting at the same time the team was  way encouraged feature for the show  Warner Brothers was contacted by an  agent representing Mark Hamill Hamill  who was a huge fan of Batman was  interested in working on the show and  Romano created a small guest role for  him in one of the episodes where Hamill  recorded the episode he'd also made it  known that what he intended was to  become a permanent member of the cast  shortly thereafter Hamill was offered  the chance to audition for the role of  the Joker but he initially shied away  from playing such an iconic role and  expressed a desire to play one of  Batman's second tier villains such as  two-face or clay face Hamill also  thought that audiences would not buy  into the idea that the actor who  portrayed one of the best and known  loved heroes in film was now playing a  super villain however figuring that he  had little chance to actually land the  role the Joker Hamill relented an  audition  [Music]  [Laughter]  [Music]  according to writer Paul Dini as soon as  Hamill perform the Joker's laugh which  captured the cruelty humour and sadness  of his character he knew that they'd  found the actor that was perfect for the  role and the decision was made to  replace curry with Hamill and so  following this other voice actors will  be added to the cast including future  Hellboy star Ron Perlman as Clayface and  Kate Mulgrew as red car the first  episode of batman the animated series  aired on the Fox Network block of  children's programming called Fox Kids  on September 5th and 1992 and aired in  the 4:30 p.m. timeslot on weekdays a  three months later Fox also began  running the show in primetime on Sunday  evenings but removed it from this  timeslot in March of 1993 as a failed to  garner the ratings they'd hoped for not  only was the show one of Fox's most  popular animated offerings among users  but is still widely regarded as the best  adaptation of Batman in any medium the  animation series contributed greatly to  the overall mythos of Batman in several  ways for example episode 3 titled heart  of ice focused on the villain mr. freeze  who was considered a lower tier member  of Batman's rogues gallery at the time  writer Paul Dini decided to expand on  freezes origin by introducing Nora the  wife of mr. freeze who become 