iginal run with 85  episodes in total and most of the  creative team began working on their  next project Superman the animated  series in 1997 the contract granting Fox  exclusive rights to the show expired and  Warner Brothers approached Bruce Timm  and making more episodes of Batman to  run alongside Superman on one of others  own network the WB both Tim and Warner  executives wanted to give the show now  titled the new Batman adventures a new  feeling and Warner Brothers was  specifically focused on increasing the  show's appeal among young audiences  Tim's approach to the network's  objective was to modify the look of the  show to be more simplified and angular  and adding more of Batman supporting  cast such as Batgirl and Nightwing into  every episode this iteration of the show  ran for 24 episodes between September  13th 1997 and January 16th 1999 before  being replaced by Batman Beyond which  focused on an older Bruce Wayne  mentoring a new Batman named Terry  McGinnis in addition to being a critical  success in a rating smash on television  Batman the Animated Series expanded into  other media as well on Christmas Day 923  Warner Brothers released a full-length  animated feature titled Batman mask of  the phantasm into theaters mask of the  phantasm is considered by many fans to  be one of the best Batman movies to date  but it was not a success of the box  office earning six million dollars just  four hundred thousand over its 5.6  million dollar budget  the animated series also spawned a  comic-book tie-in to Batman adventures  which ran for a number of years in  addition to these endeavors Batman the  Animated Series also served as a  foundation and launching point for an  entire connected universe of animated  shows including Superman the animated  series Batman Beyond  Justice League and Justice League  Unlimited perhaps the best indication of  the legacy of Batman the Animated Series  lies not in its vast info  it's phenomenal critical reception  whether two Emmy Awards at garner but in  the fact that 25 years after the end of  its original run Batman the a minute  series continues to set the benchmark  for animated adaptations of coming up  with properties among fans who still  adore the show well into their adulthood  [Music]  [Music]

